{"name":"Ginger Spice","hex":"#b65d48","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ginger","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The pungent aromatic rhizome of a tropical Asian herb, Zingiber officinale, used as a spice and as a stimulant and acarminative.","The plant that produces this rhizome."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a reddish-brown color.","Having hair or fur of this color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ginger"},{"term":"spice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Aromatic or pungent plant matter (usually dried) used to season or flavor food.","The quality of being spicy."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To add spice or spices to; season.","To spice up."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Geri Halliwell","blocks":[{"text":"Geraldine Estelle Halliwell-Horner is an English singer, television personality, author, and actress. She rose to fame in the mid-1990s as a member of the pop group the Spice Girls, in which she was nicknamed Ginger Spice. With over 100 million records sold worldwide, the Spice Girls are the best-selling female group of all time. Their slogan \"girl power\" was most closely associated with Halliwell and her Union Jack dress from the 1997 Brit Awards also became an enduring symbol."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/SpiceGirlWembley150619-69_%2849000357276%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-SpiceGirlWembley150619-69_%2849000357276%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geri_Halliwell","wikidata":"Q19845"},{"title":"Ginger","blocks":[{"text":"Ginger is a flowering plant whose rhizome, ginger root or ginger, is widely used as a spice and a folk medicine. It is an herbaceous perennial that grows annual pseudostems about one meter tall, bearing narrow leaf blades. The inflorescences bear flowers having pale yellow petals with purple edges, and arise directly from the rhizome on separate shoots."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Koeh-146-no_text.jpg/330px-Koeh-146-no_text.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ginger","wikidata":"Q35625"},{"title":"Spice","blocks":[{"text":"In the culinary arts, a spice is a seed, fruit, root, bark, or other plant substance primarily used for flavouring or colouring food. Spices are distinguished from herbs, which are the leaves, flowers, or stems of plants used for flavouring or as a garnish. Spices and herbs are both seasonings. \nSpices are sometimes used in medicine, religious rituals, cosmetics, or perfume production. They are usually classified into spices, spice seeds, and herbal categories. For example, vanilla is commonly used as an ingredient in fragrance manufacturing. Plant-based sweeteners such as sugar are not considered spices."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Spices1.jpg/330px-Spices1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spice","wikidata":"Q42527"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Geri_Halliwell_in_concert_cropped.jpg/500px-Geri_Halliwell_in_concert_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Geri_Halliwell_in_concert_cropped.jpg/500px-Geri_Halliwell_in_concert_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Halliwell in 2008 wearing a remake of her Union Jack dress from the 1997 Brit Awards","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeri_Halliwell_in_concert_cropped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Geri_Halliwell_in_concert_%282007%29_%283%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Geri_Halliwell_in_concert_%282007%29_%283%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Geri_Halliwell_in_concert_%282007%29_%283%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Geri_Halliwell_in_concert_%282007%29_%283%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Halliwell performing \"It's Raining Men\", her fourth number-one single, on the Return of The Spice Girls Tour","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeri_Halliwell_in_concert_(2007)_(3)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/GeriHalliwellASDA1.JPG/330px-GeriHalliwellASDA1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/GeriHalliwellASDA1.JPG/330px-GeriHalliwellASDA1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Halliwell at a book signing in 2008","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeriHalliwellASDA1.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/SpiceGirlWembley150619-22_%2849000567242%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-SpiceGirlWembley150619-22_%2849000567242%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/SpiceGirlWembley150619-22_%2849000567242%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-SpiceGirlWembley150619-22_%2849000567242%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/SpiceGirlWembley150619-22_%2849000567242%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-SpiceGirlWembley150619-22_%2849000567242%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Halliwell during Spice World – 2019 Tour, June 2019","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpice